text:
tay: Quick UX/Accessibility question: should we add a keyboard shortcut to copy the correlation ID when focused in the trace detail? Thinking Cmd/Ctrl+C when the corr-id element is focused, plus a visible tooltip hint: 'Press ⌘C to copy'. Figma: https://www.figma.com/file/shortcut-copy-corrid

leo: I like the discoverability angle. Two notes: 1) need to avoid capturing global Cmd/Ctrl+C if user is editing elsewhere. 2) fallback must be a visible copy button for mouse and keyboard.

sam: Implementation: detect focus on corr-id element and then intercept copy only for that element (preventDefault + write to clipboard). Also expose an aria-describedby that points to the tooltip text so screen readers announce the shortcut.

marie: A11y: Keyboard shortcut hints are helpful, but do not rely on them. For screen reader users, add a dedicated "Copy correlation ID" button (in DOM order right after the ID). Ensure the button has aria-label="Copy correlation ID" and the toast uses role=status + aria-live=polite: "Correlation ID copied to clipboard."

leo: Also consider a small permalink action: 'Copy trace permalink' which copies a deep link (shortened). Should the permalink be in the kebab or alongside copy ID? My vote: keep permalink in kebab to avoid clutter; show a short URL preview in the detail header when a user clicks "Share".

tay: Good call. For mobile, we should show a long-press context menu on the corr-id with copy and share. Desktop gets visible button + shortcut hint.

sam: Analytics events: trace.copy_via_shortcut, trace.copy_via_button, trace.copy_permalink (props: trace_id, source:list|detail, user_agent). Also track user flow where they use cmd/ctrl-c vs button to see adoption.

marie: Small code snippet suggestion for clipboard handling:

<code>
const idEl = document.querySelector('[data-trace-id]');
idEl.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === 'c') {
    e.preventDefault();
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(idEl.dataset.traceId).then(() => announce('Correlation ID copied'));
  }
});
</code>

leo: Testing notes: validate with VoiceOver, NVDA, and TalkBack. Check that aria-describedby announces the shortcut only when appropriate. Also ensure focus styles are visible (2px high-contrast ring).

a11y-bot: Created tickets: UX-3301 (Shortcut + copy button), UX-3302 (Permalink in kebab), UX-3303 (Mobile long-press menu) :rocket:

tay: Action items: tay update figma with shortcut hint and long-press spec by Fri; sam to prototype keyboard handler and analytics by Tue; marie to draft SR-friendly toast message and a11y checklist by Wed.

leo: One more microcopy decision: visible hint text should read 'Press ⌘C to copy' on macOS and 'Press Ctrl+C to copy' on Windows. Use platform detection to show correct glyph.

marie: I'll add that to the accessibility docs. Closing thread, will reopen with prototype links.
